              "type": "text",
              "content": "Curiosity | Textbook of Science| Grade 6"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.092,
            0.883,
            0.135
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Correct way of measuring temperature using a laboratory thermometer"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.144,
            0.546,
            0.421
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 2,
              "bbox": [
                0.112,
                0.144,
                0.546,
                0.421
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_9_image_2.jpg",
              "content": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "image_caption",
              "index": 3,
              "bbox": [
                0.14,
                0.428,
                0.522,
                0.447
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Fig.7.4: Measuring temperature of warm water"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.58,
            0.139,
            0.884,
            0.243
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "When the thermometer is immersed in water, its bulb should not touch the bottom or the sides of the beaker."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.581,
            0.247,
            0.851,
            0.33
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The thermometer should be held vertically (Fig. 7.4). It should not be tilted."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.581,
            0.334,
            0.834,
            0.418
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The temperature must be read while the thermometer is immersed in water."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.583,
            0.421,
            0.883,
            0.463
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "While reading the thermometer, the eye"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.462,
            0.883,
            0.505
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "should be directly in line with the level of the liquid column to be read (Fig. 7.4)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.255,
            0.519,
            0.552,
            0.541
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Activity 7.5: Let us measure"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.104,
            0.892,
            0.139,
            0.908
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "132"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.551,
            0.679,
            0.572
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Take some warm water in a beaker."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.577,
            0.883,
            0.619
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Dip the thermometer in water so that the bulb is immersed in water (Fig. 7.4)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.624,
            0.871,
            0.645
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Observe the rise of liquid column in the thermometer."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.155,
            0.657,
            0.394,
            0.91
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 14,
              "bbox": [
                0.155,
                0.657,
                0.394,
                0.91
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_9_image_14.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.401,
            0.653,
            0.883,
            0.714
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Wait till the column stops rising and note the temperature (do not wait too long; otherwise, the water itself will start to cool)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.401,
            0.715,
            0.883,
            0.776
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What is the temperature of water measured by you? Compare it with the readings of your friends."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.352,
            0.776,
            0.883,
            0.837
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Do you notice that, as soon as you take the thermometer out of the water, the level of liquid column begins to fall?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.35,
            0.837,
            0.882,
            0.879
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "This means that the temperature must be read while the thermometer is immersed in water."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.449,
            0.97,
            0.551,
            0.985
          ],
